1-5 Purpose of the article
The purpose of this article is to comprehensively examine the impact of metaverse on learning processes. In this regard, the present study, with a mixed approach (review and empirical), has both analyzed the content of international scientific research and examined the empirical data obtained from the questionnaire.The article attempts to answer these questions:
1. How can the metaverse improve the quality of learning and the mental engagement of learners?
2. What changes in users’ mental habits, focus, and motivation occur as a result of the metaverse experience?
3. What are the key challenges and opportunities for using the metaverse in education?

2- Metaverse and Education
2-1- Definition of Metaverse
A metaverse is a digital and virtual world in which users can interact, learn, and gain new experiences through their avatars. This simulated environment is created through a combination of virtual reality (VR), augmented reality (AR), and artificial intelligence (AI), and provides an interactive and multisensory platform for social, educational, and recreational activities (Bailenson, 2018).
2-2- Metaverse as a platform for innovation and transformation
The metaverse can bring about significant changes in educational systems. In these virtual spaces, individuals can connect with others through their avatars and have deep learning experiences that go beyond physical limitations. Education in the metaverse provides opportunities for learning in interactive and engaging environments. In the metaverse, simulated environments can be created for practical and workshop training that take the learning experience beyond traditional methods.
2-3- Features of the metaverse in education
2-3-1- Interactive and group learning: Students can interact in group environments such as virtual classes or science projects. Traditional educational methods often rely on passive learning, where students receive information without active interaction. In contrast, the metaverse actively engages users in simulated environments by creating experiential and collaborative learning (Johnson et al., 2023). For example, instead of simply studying about World War I, students can experience a 3D simulation of the war and gain a deeper understanding of history.
2-3-2-Multisensory Interaction and Immersive Interaction: The use of virtual reality (VR) and augmented reality (AR) technologies transforms learning into a multidimensional experience that engages multiple senses simultaneously (Slater & Sanchez-Vives, 2016).
2-3-3- Simulated Training: One of the most important benefits of the metaverse is the possibility of interactive simulation, which allows learners to practice complex skills in environments that are dangerous or difficult in the real world.
Examples of this type of training include: chemical experiments in a virtual environment without the hazards of real chemicals, flight simulation for pilot students, medical and surgical training for medical students, crisis management in emergency situations and emergencies.
Research shows that the use of virtual reality technologies in educational environments increases student engagement and learning (Li et al., 2022).
2-3-4-Reducing geographical and economic barriers: One of the challenges of traditional education systems is geographical and economic limitations. The metaverse can eliminate these barriers. For example, many people around the world may not have access to reputable universities or quality educational opportunities. But in the metaverse, anyone with an internet connection can attend authentic educational classes.
Studies have shown that the metaverse can provide access to quality education for people living in disadvantaged areas (Pereira et al., 2023).
2-3-5- Personalized Learning: The metaverse allows for the personalization of the learning experience, meaning that learning environments can be designed based on the specific needs of each student.
Artificial intelligence (AI)-based algorithms can analyze student progress and tailor lessons to their learning styles. Studies show that AI-based educational platforms in the metaverse improve learning outcomes. (Zhu et al., 2023).
In traditional classrooms, all students must learn at the same pace and in the same way, but in the metaverse, learners can progress at their own pace and interests, which increases their motivation and engagement in the learning process.
2-3-6- Strengthening social skills through avatars: Interaction in metaverse environments can strengthen the communication skills of children and adults.
2-3-7- Social learning: In the metaverse, individuals can participate in classes, seminars, and workshops simultaneously. Students can participate in interactive virtual classes, ask questions, and solve complex problems in groups. Research has shown that social learning in the metaverse can improve students’ communication and collaboration skills (Dillenbourg et al., 2021).
2-3-8- Game-Based Learning: Another transformative aspect of the metaverse in education is game-based learning. Educational games in the metaverse enable students to learn new concepts in an interactive and fun way. Research has shown that educational games can increase student engagement and make learning more effective (Johnson et al., 2021).
2-3-9- Visualization: The metaverse can help learners see things that were previously difficult to see in the real world, such as molecules or biological cells (Thopsou., 2021). In addition, it can simulate ideal conditions in physics and make abstract theories tangible, for example Einstein's theory of relativity (Georgiu et., 2021).
This type of learning can also strengthen critical thinking and problem-solving skills in students.
 
